  {
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "@Qu-Xiangjun I believe I\u2019ve figured out the root cause \u2014 it\u2019s due to floating-point rounding errors introduced during the atomic additions in the Split-K reduction. When SPLIT_K=1 or the tutorial code, the results are consistent because the accumulation is performed in a single pass without atomic operations. However, when SPLIT_K > 1, partial results are accumulated separately and merged via atomic_add, which can lead to minor differences.",
